                        "glosses": [
                            "A contract preceding another, especially a contract of marriage which, according to the ancient law, rendered void a subsequent marriage solemnized in violation of it."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "5dd47647-60cc-4812-bfdb-9d54961bd8ff",
                                "sense_id": "c4c9751d-95c0-3a74-9e1b-76bdd092cd28",
                                "text": "Two grounds are surmised , by opposite parties : a pre-contract with Percy , Earl of Northumberland ; and an adulterous intercourse of Henry , many years preceding , with Anne's sister , Mary Boleyn."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "33b68378-e586-40ea-ac07-2bb2c774d69c",
                                "sense_id": "c4c9751d-95c0-3a74-9e1b-76bdd092cd28",
                                "text": "A followed in the Federal courts , to the precontract , valid by the Constitution and laws judice of holders for value who acquired their of a State"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
